<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Saud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1765">1765</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Saud was emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> from 1727 and the founder of the first Saudi state. In 1744 he made a pact with the religious reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a>, joining political power to the Wahhabi movement. The alliance launched the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Diriyah, and his descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">House of Saud</a>, rule Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> today.</p></div>
